        {
          "path": "_m/r/r/k/0/bombing-of-rabaul-november-1943-wp/hero.jpg",
          "filename": "Japanese cruiser Haguro at Rabaul.jpg",
          "caption": "Aircraft of the USAAF 3rd Bomb Group attack Japanese ships in Simpson Harbor, 2 November 1943.\n\nThe heavy cruiser Haguro is in the foreground. She had been somewhat damaged during the battle of Empress Augusta Bay the previous night. The burning transport at right appears to be one of the Hakone Maru class, of which Hakone Maru, Hakozaki Maru and Hakusan Maru were still afloat at the time. The ship in the left distance, partially hidden by smoke, appears to be the submarine tender Chogei or Jingei.",
